          content: `# Building a Data Layer

## 📚 What You'll Learn
- Build a complete data access layer for an e-commerce app
- Implement complex queries with relationships
- Handle transactions and concurrent access

## 🎯 Challenge: E-Commerce Data Layer

### Entity Model:
- User — id, name, email, password, createdAt
- Product — id, name, description, price, quantity, sku, createdAt
- Category — id, name, description
- Order — id, user (ManyToOne), total, status, orderDate
- OrderItem — id, order (ManyToOne), product (ManyToOne), quantity, unitPrice
- Review — id, user (ManyToOne), product (ManyToOne), rating, comment, createdAt

### Requirements:
1. Define entities with relationships and cascade types
2. Repositories with custom queries (pagination, rating, top-selling)
3. Transaction management with pessimistic locking for stock`,
          codeTemplate: "// TODO: Build e-commerce data layer\n// 1. Define entities with relationships\n// 2. Create repositories\n// 3. Implement OrderService with transactions",
          solution: `@Entity
@Table(name = "products")
public class Product {
    @Id @GeneratedValue(strategy = GenerationType.IDENTITY)
    private Long id;
    @NotBlank @Column(nullable = false)
    private String name;
    @Positive @Column(nullable = false)
    private BigDecimal price;
    @Min(0) @Column(nullable = false)
    private int quantity;
    @ManyToMany
    @JoinTable(name = "product_category",
        joinColumns = @JoinColumn(name = "product_id"),
        inverseJoinColumns = @JoinColumn(name = "category_id"))
    private Set<Category> categories = new HashSet<>();
    @OneToMany(mappedBy = "product", cascade = CascadeType.ALL)
    private List<Review> reviews = new ArrayList<>();
    @Version
    private Long version;
}

public interface ProductRepository extends JpaRepository<Product, Long> {
    Page<Product> findByCategory(String category, Pageable pageable);
    @Query("SELECT AVG(r.rating) FROM Review r WHERE r.product.id = :productId")
    Double findAverageRating(@Param("productId") Long productId);
    @Lock(LockModeType.PESSIMISTIC_WRITE)
    @Query("SELECT p FROM Product p WHERE p.id = :id")
    Optional<Product> findByIdWithLock(@Param("id") Long id);
    @Query("SELECT p FROM Product p ORDER BY (SELECT COALESCE(SUM(oi.quantity), 0) FROM OrderItem oi WHERE oi.product.id = p.id) DESC")
    Page<Product> findTopSelling(Pageable pageable);
}

@Service
public class OrderService {
    @Transactional(isolation = Isolation.REPEATABLE_READ)
    public Order placeOrder(Long userId, List<OrderItemRequest> items) {
        BigDecimal total = BigDecimal.ZERO;
        List<OrderItem> orderItems = new ArrayList<>();
        for (OrderItemRequest req : items) {
            Product product = productRepository.findByIdWithLock(req.productId()).orElseThrow();
            if (product.getQuantity() < req.quantity())
                throw new RuntimeException("Insufficient stock");
            product.setQuantity(product.getQuantity() - req.quantity());
            total = total.add(product.getPrice().multiply(BigDecimal.valueOf(req.quantity())));
            orderItems.add(new OrderItem(product, req.quantity(), product.getPrice()));
        }
        Order order = new Order(userId, total, "PENDING", LocalDateTime.now(), orderItems);
        orderItems.forEach(oi -> oi.setOrder(order));
        return orderRepository.save(order);
    }
}`,
