          title: "Distributed Tracing & Resilience",
          type: "challenge",
          content: `# Distributed Tracing & Resilience

## 📚 Learn: Micrometer Tracing, Resilience4j patterns, Zipkin

## 🎯 Challenge: Build Resilient Microservices System

### Requirements:
1. Distributed Tracing with Micrometer + Zipkin (single traceId across services)
2. Circuit Breaker (50% failure opens circuit, fallback returns cached data)
3. Retry with exponential backoff (3 attempts, 5xx only)
4. Bulkhead (max 10 concurrent calls to inventory)
5. Rate Limiter (100 requests/min per user)
6. Metrics exposed via Actuator

### Bonus: Chaos engineering endpoint for testing failures`,
          codeTemplate: "// TODO: Implement tracing and resilience\n// 1. Micrometer Tracing + Zipkin\n// 2. Resilience4j circuit breaker + retry + bulkhead\n// 3. Custom health indicators showing downstream status",
          solution: `// Resilience4j Configuration
@Service
public class ResilientInventoryClient {
    @Autowired private InventoryClient client;

    @CircuitBreaker(name = "inventory", fallbackMethod = "fallback")
    @Retry(name = "inventory-retry")
    @Bulkhead(name = "inventory-bulkhead", type = Bulkhead.Type.THREADPOOL)
    @RateLimiter(name = "inventory-ratelimit")
    @TimeLimiter(name = "inventory-timeout")
    public CompletableFuture<DeductResponse> deductStock(DeductRequest req) {
        return CompletableFuture.supplyAsync(() -> client.deductStock(req));
    }

    public CompletableFuture<DeductResponse> fallback(DeductRequest req, Throwable t) {
        return CompletableFuture.completedFuture(new DeductResponse(req.productId(), req.quantity(), true, "CACHED"));
    }
}

# application.yml
resilience4j:
  circuitbreaker:
    instances:
      inventory:
        sliding-window-size: 10
        minimum-number-of-calls: 5
        failure-rate-threshold: 50
        wait-duration-in-open-state: 10s
        permitted-number-of-calls-in-half-open-state: 3
  retry:
    instances:
      inventory-retry:
        max-attempts: 3
        wait-duration: 500ms
        exponential-backoff-multiplier: 2
        retry-exceptions: org.springframework.web.client.HttpServerErrorException
  bulkhead:
    instances:
      inventory-bulkhead:
        max-concurrent-calls: 10
        max-wait-duration: 500ms

# Tracing (in each service)
management.tracing.sampling.probability: 1.0
management.zipkin.tracing.endpoint: http://localhost:9411/api/v2/spans

# Custom health indicator
@Component
public class DownstreamHealth implements HealthIndicator {
    @Override public Health health() {
        Map<String, Object> details = new HashMap<>();
        try { inventoryClient.health(); details.put("inventory", "UP"); }
        catch (Exception e) { details.put("inventory", "DOWN"); }
        try { paymentClient.health(); details.put("payment", "UP"); }
        catch (Exception e) { details.put("payment", "DOWN"); }
        boolean allUp = details.values().stream().allMatch(v -> v.equals("UP"));
        return allUp ? Health.up().withDetails(details).build() : Health.down().withDetails(details).build();
    }
}`,
