          title: "Circuit Breakers with Resilience4j",
          type: "practice",
          content: `# Circuit Breakers with Resilience4j

## 📚 Learn: Circuit breaker, retry, bulkhead, rate limiter patterns

## 📖 Explanation
Circuit breakers prevent cascading failures. If a service is failing, the circuit opens and subsequent calls fail immediately (or use fallback) instead of waiting for a timeout.

## 🛠️ Practice: Configure Resilience4j patterns for a payment service call`,
          codeTemplate: "// TODO: Add Resilience4j patterns to PaymentClient\n// 1. Circuit breaker (50% failure rate opens circuit)\n// 2. Retry (3 attempts, exponential backoff)\n// 3. Bulkhead (max 5 concurrent calls)\n// 4. Time limiter (2s timeout)\n// 5. Rate limiter (100 req/min)",
          solution: `@Service
public class ResilientPaymentClient {
    @Autowired private PaymentClient client;

    @CircuitBreaker(name = "payment", fallbackMethod = "paymentFallback")
    @Retry(name = "payment-retry")
    @Bulkhead(name = "payment-bulkhead", type = Bulkhead.Type.THREADPOOL)
    @RateLimiter(name = "payment-rate-limit")
    @TimeLimiter(name = "payment-timeout")
    public CompletableFuture<PaymentResponse> processPayment(PaymentRequest req) {
        return CompletableFuture.supplyAsync(() -> client.charge(req));
    }

    public CompletableFuture<PaymentResponse> paymentFallback(PaymentRequest req, Throwable t) {
        log.warn("Payment service unavailable, queuing for retry: {}", t.getMessage());
        paymentRetryQueue.add(req); // Queue for later retry
        return CompletableFuture.completedFuture(new PaymentResponse("PENDING", "Queued for retry"));
    }
}

# application.yml
resilience4j:
  circuitbreaker:
    instances:
      payment:
        sliding-window-size: 10
        minimum-number-of-calls: 5
        failure-rate-threshold: 50
        wait-duration-in-open-state: 15s
        permitted-number-of-calls-in-half-open-state: 3
  retry:
    instances:
      payment-retry:
        max-attempts: 3
        wait-duration: 1s
        exponential-backoff-multiplier: 2
        retry-exceptions: org.springframework.web.client.HttpServerErrorException
        ignore-exceptions: org.springframework.web.client.HttpClientErrorException
  bulkhead:
    instances:
      payment-bulkhead:
        max-concurrent-calls: 5
        max-wait-duration: 500ms
  ratelimiter:
    instances:
      payment-rate-limit:
        limit-for-period: 100
        limit-refresh-period: 60s
        timeout-duration: 5s
  timelimiter:
    instances:
      payment-timeout:
        timeout-duration: 2s

# Metrics exposure
management.endpoints.web.exposure.include: health,info,circuitbreakers,retries,bulkheads,ratelimiters`,
