              code: "# Development: deploy on every PR merge\nbranches: [main] → Deploy to dev cluster\n\n# Staging: manual trigger for pre-release testing\nworkflow_dispatch: → Deploy to staging cluster\n  inputs:\n    tag: { description: 'Docker tag to deploy' }\n\n# Production: manual approval after staging tests\nenvironment:\n  name: production\n  url: https://myapp.com\n\n# Rollback on health check failure\n- name: Verify deployment\n  run: |\n    for i in {1..30}; do\n      STATUS=$(kubectl get pods -l app=order-service -o jsonpath='{.items[0].status.containerStatuses[0].ready}')\n      if [ \"$STATUS\" = \"true\" ]; then exit 0; fi\n      sleep 2\n    done\n    kubectl rollout undo deployment/order-service\n    exit 1",
              explanation: "Multi-environment pipelines promote code through environments with increasing validation. Production deploys require manual approval. Rollback is automatic on deploy failure.",
              difficulty: "intermediate"
