          title: "Production Hardening & Best Practices",
          type: "challenge",
          content: `# Production Hardening & Best Practices

## 📚 Learn: Security, performance, reliability, and observability for production

## 🎯 Challenge: Harden a Spring Boot App for Production

### Security:
1. All secrets in environment variables or Vault (never in code)
2. HTTPS enabled (TLS 1.3)
3. Security headers: CSP, HSTS, X-Frame-Options, X-Content-Type-Options
4. Rate limiting on login endpoint (5 attempts/min per IP)
5. SQL injection protection (already safe with JPA, verify)
6. Dependency vulnerability scanning (OWASP plugin)

### Performance:
1. Connection pooling (HikariCP) optimized: max=20, min=5, timeout=30s
2. Redis caching for frequently accessed data
3. GZip compression on responses
4. Static resource caching (Cache-Control, ETag)
5. Database query optimization (indexes, @Query optimization)

### Reliability:
1. Graceful shutdown (spring.lifecycle.timeout-per-shutdown-phase=30s)
2. Health checks for all dependencies
3. Circuit breakers for all external calls
4. Retry with backoff for transient failures
5. Rate limiting for public endpoints

### Observability:
1. Structured JSON logging with correlation IDs
2. Distributed tracing (Zipkin) for all services
3. Prometheus metrics + Grafana dashboards
4. Centralized log aggregation (ELK)
5. Alerts for: high error rate, high latency, low disk

### Bonus: Penetration test, chaos engineering, load test`,
          codeTemplate: "// TODO: Harden Spring Boot app for production\n// 1. Enable HTTPS and security headers\n// 2. Configure HikariCP connection pool\n// 3. Add Redis caching\n// 4. Enable graceful shutdown\n// 5. Configure structured JSON logging\n// 6. Add dependency vulnerability scanning",
          solution: `# ========== Security Configuration ==========
@Configuration
public class SecurityConfig {
    @Bean
    public SecurityFilterChain filterChain(HttpSecurity http) throws Exception {
        http
            .headers(headers -> headers
                .contentSecurityPolicy(csp -> csp.policyDirectives("default-src 'self'"))
                .httpStrictTransportSecurity(hsts -> hsts.maxAgeInSeconds(31536000).includeSubDomains(true))
                .frameOptions(frame -> frame.deny())
                .contentTypeOptions(content -> content.disable())
            )
            .requiresChannel(channel -> channel.anyRequest().requiresSecure()) // HTTPS only
            .sessionManagement(session -> session.sessionCreationPolicy(SessionCreationPolicy.STATELESS))
            .authorizeHttpRequests(auth -> auth
                .requestMatchers("/actuator/health").permitAll()
                .anyRequest().authenticated()
            );
        return http.build();
    }

    @Bean
    public RateLimiter loginRateLimiter() {
        return new InMemoryRateLimiter(5, Duration.ofMinutes(1)); // 5 attempts/min/IP
    }
}

# ========== application-prod.yml ==========
# Performance
spring.datasource.hikari:
  maximum-pool-size: 20
  minimum-idle: 5
  connection-timeout: 30000
  idle-timeout: 600000
  max-lifetime: 1800000

spring.cache:
  type: redis
  redis.time-to-live: 60000

server.compression:
  enabled: true
  mime-types: text/html,text/plain,text/css,application/javascript,application/json
  min-response-size: 1024

server.tomcat.connection-timeout: 5s

# Reliability
spring.lifecycle.timeout-per-shutdown-phase: 30s

# Logging
logging.pattern.console: "%d{ISO8601} [%X{traceId:-}] [%X{userId:-}] %-5level %logger{36} - %msg%n"

# ========== Docker Compose with Security Scanning ==========
# pom.xml — OWASP dependency check
<plugin>
    <groupId>org.owasp</groupId>
    <artifactId>dependency-check-maven</artifactId>
    <version>9.0.9</version>
    <configuration>
        <failBuildOnCVSS>7</failBuildOnCVSS> <!-- Fail on high severity -->
    </configuration>
</plugin>

# ========== Load Testing with k6 ==========
import http from 'k6/http';
import { check, sleep } from 'k6';

export let options = {
    stages: [
        { duration: '2m', target: 100 },  // Ramp up to 100 users
        { duration: '5m', target: 100 },  // Stay at 100
        { duration: '2m', target: 200 },  // Spike to 200
        { duration: '2m', target: 0 },    // Scale down
    ],
    thresholds: {
        http_req_duration: ['p(95)<2000'], // 95% requests under 2s
        http_req_failed: ['rate<0.01'],    // <1% failure rate
    },
};

export default function () {
    let res = http.get('http://localhost:8080/api/products');
    check(res, { 'status is 200': (r) => r.status === 200 });
    sleep(1);
}`,
