          content: `# Introduction to CSS

📚 What You'll Learn
- What CSS is and how it works with HTML
- The three ways to add CSS: inline, internal, and external
- CSS syntax: selectors, properties, and values
- Basic color and background properties

📖 Simple Explanation
CSS (Cascading Style Sheets) is like the "clothing" for your HTML skeleton. HTML provides the structure, and CSS makes it look good. You can change colors, fonts, spacing, and layout. The "cascading" part means styles can flow from parent to child elements, and more specific rules override general ones.

🎯 Why This Matters
Without CSS, every website would look like a plain text document with Times New Roman on a white background. CSS is what makes the web visually appealing and user-friendly. It's the difference between a boring document and a professional website.`,
