          title: "The CSS Box Model",
          type: "theory",
          content: `# The CSS Box Model

📚 What You'll Learn
- Understanding the four layers: content, padding, border, margin
- How box-sizing affects element dimensions
- Using width, height, and max-width properties
- Controlling spacing between and within elements

📖 Simple Explanation
Every HTML element is a rectangular box. The box model is like a package: you have the item itself (content), bubble wrap around it (padding), the box it's in (border), and space between this box and other boxes (margin). Padding pushes content inward, margin pushes other elements away. Understanding this is crucial because it determines how elements are sized and spaced on your page.

🎯 Why This Matters
The box model is one of the most fundamental concepts in CSS. Misunderstanding it leads to layout disasters - elements that don't fit, unexpected gaps, and overflowing content. Mastering the box model gives you precise control over spacing and sizing.`,
