          type: "theory",
          content: `# Introduction to Flexbox

📚 What You'll Learn
- What Flexbox is and what problems it solves
- The main axis and cross axis concept
- Flex container and flex item properties
- Aligning, justifying, and distributing items

📖 Simple Explanation
Flexbox is a CSS layout model designed for one-dimensional layouts (rows or columns). Imagine items on a shelf: Flexbox helps you control how they're arranged (left to right or top to bottom), how they're spaced (with gaps or pushed to ends), and how they respond to different container sizes. It's like having an intelligent shelf that automatically adjusts spacing when you add or remove items.

🎯 Why This Matters
Before Flexbox, creating centered layouts or equal-height columns required hacks and workarounds. Flexbox simplifies these common layout patterns dramatically. It's the go-to solution for navigation bars, card layouts, centered content, and any row/column-based arrangement.`,
