              title: "Basic CSS Grid",
              description: "Creating a simple grid layout",
              code: ".grid {\n  display: grid;\n  grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr 1fr;  /* Three equal columns */\n  gap: 20px;\n}\n\n.item {\n  background: #e74c3c;\n  color: white;\n  padding: 30px;\n  text-align: center;\n  border-radius: 5px;\n}\n\n/* HTML:\n<div class=\"grid\">\n  <div class=\"item\">1</div>\n  <div class=\"item\">2</div>\n  <div class=\"item\">3</div>\n  <div class=\"item\">4</div>\n  <div class=\"item\">5</div>\n  <div class=\"item\">6</div>\n</div>\n*/",
              explanation: "grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr 1fr creates 3 equal-width columns. Items fill cells left-to-right, top-to-bottom. The gap property creates consistent spacing. fr units distribute remaining space, similar to flex: 1.",
